Module 4: List & Multimedia Control(Advanced Attributes)

web pages par content ko thode organize tarike se dikhane ke liye list aur media use hote hian.

1.List Types
:Unordered List (<ul>): Bullet points ke liye. Iska default style dot(disc) hota hai. Par hum css se ise badal skte hain.
:Ordered List (<ol>): Isme numbering hoti hain. HTML5 mein iske Pass kuch cool Attributes hain:
    :: <ol type="A"> ->>Ab numbering 1,2,3 ki jagah A B c mein aayegi
                    (type="i" se roman numbers ban jayege).
    :: <ol start="5"> ->> numbering seedhe 5 se shuru hogi (5,6,7..).

<ol type="I" start="3">
    <li>HTML Core</li> <!-- Yeh III dikhayega -->
    <li>CSS Styling</li> <!-- Yeh IV dikhayega -->
</ol>


2.Multimedia Deep Control (<Video> & <audio>)
Apne phele video lagana seekha, ab uske Advanced Attributes dekhiye jo badi websites use karti hain:

::autoplay: Page load hote ki video apne aap chalne lagegi.
::muted : Video bina aawaz ke shuru hogi.(Note: Aaj kal ke browsers bina
        muted ke autoplay allow nahi karte, taaki user pareshan na ho).

::loop : Video khatam hote he apne aap dobara shuru hojayegi (jaise 
        Instagram reels).
:: poster="...": Video chalne se phele jo thumbnail phto dikhti hai, wo
            is Attributes se lagti hai.


<video controls autoplay muted loop poster="thumbnail.jpg" width="600">
    <source src="course-video.mp4" type="video/mp4">
</video>

